<title>GERMANY: Hoechst continues descent in IBIS trade.</title>
<headline>Hoechst continues descent in IBIS trade.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG on Thursday continued falling after 1996 business results published earlier this week and market disappointment over a decision to shelve the flotation of its HMR unit.</p>
<p>In pre-bourse IBIS trade, Hoechst shares fell 1.84 marks ($1.08) to 67.30 on volume of 523,000 shares. Dealers said, however, they did not think a sell-off on the scale of Wednesday, when the stock fell over 10 percent in bourse trade, was likely.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.695 German Marks)</p>
